Package: estheRineq
Type: Package
Title: Epidemiological Statistics Toolkit for Health Inequality Estimation and Reporting
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Akram",
    family = "Hernández-Vásquez",
    role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "akram.hernandez.v@gmail.com",
    comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1431-2526")
  )
Description: Unites complex-survey health econometrics and epidemiological health
    inequality surveillance and reporting. Provides rank-dependent concentration
    indices (standard, generalized, modified, Wagstaff, Erreygers, extended, and
    symmetric) with exact Gateaux influence-function linearization, stratified
    multistage ultimate-cluster variance, replicate weights, and Rao-Wu-Yue
    survey bootstrap inference following O'Donnell, O'Neill, Van Ourti, and Walsh
    (2016) <doi:10.1177/1536867X1601600112>; classical univariate inequality
    indices (Gini, S-Gini, Atkinson, generalized entropy, Palma, S80/S20) and
    subgroup decompositions; all 21 World Health Organization Health Inequality
    Monitor summary measures following Schlotheuber and Hosseinpoor (2022)
    <doi:10.3390/ijerph191912592>; modern logistic and modified-Poisson slope and
    relative indices of inequality ('SII' and 'RII') following Moreno-Betancur et
    al. (2015) <doi:10.1093/ije/dyv148>; direct and indirect epidemiological rate
    standardization with Dobson and Byar confidence intervals; econometric
    health-need standardization and horizontal inequity; reference-invariant
    Wagstaff, recentered influence-function ('RIF'), and counterfactual
    'RIF'-Oaxaca decompositions; editorial visualizations (Pelotas 'equiplots',
    concentration curves, gradient plots, decomposition forest plots, and
    Spiegelhalter funnel plots); and multilingual (English, Spanish, Portuguese)
    'STROBE'-Equity exports following Dewidar, Welch, et al. (2025)
    <doi:10.1136/bmj-2024-083882>.
